.TH CARGO-FMT 1 "September 2026" "Rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cargo-fmt \- format a Cargo package with rustfmt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cargo fmt
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR rustfmt-options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cargo fmt
formats the binary and library targets of a Cargo package using
.BR rustfmt (1).
It obtains target paths and language editions from Cargo metadata.
By default, files are rewritten. Configuration is read by rustfmt from
.B rustfmt.toml
or
.BR .rustfmt.toml .
.PP
The installed
.B cargo-fmt
executable implements the Cargo
.B fmt
subcommand. Arguments after
.B \-\-
are passed to rustfmt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check formatting without rewriting files. Return a nonzero status if changes
are required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-package " " \fIpackage\fR...
Select the package or packages to format.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Format all packages and their local path dependencies.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest\-path " path"
Use the Cargo manifest at
.IR path ,
which must name a
.B Cargo.toml
file.
.TP
.BI \-\-message\-format " short|json|human"
Select the report format. JSON output cannot be combined with check mode
or an explicit rustfmt
.B \-\-emit
option.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress standard output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show additional information. Do not combine with
.BR \-\-quiet .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the rustfmt version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTFMT
Override the rustfmt executable used by Cargo's formatter integration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates an error or formatting differences
in check mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
Format the current package:
.PP
.nf
cargo fmt
.fi
.PP
Check all packages and local path dependencies:
.PP
.nf
cargo fmt \-\-all \-\-check
.fi
.PP
Pass a formatting option to rustfmt:
.PP
.nf
cargo fmt \-\- \-\-config max_width=100
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo (1),
.BR rustfmt (1)
.PP
https://rust-lang.github.io/rustfmt/
